# Commercial S10.2C Telegram channel administrator-rights diagnosis

## Finding

The first live S10.2B cutover preflight on 2026-09-04 stopped before quiescing
or changing any public service. Both the new and legacy bots had exactly the
three rights exposed and selected in Telegram Desktop for the existing
`@WantMeSeen` broadcast channel: change channel information, post messages and
edit messages. Delete, invite, story, video-chat, direct-message and
administrator-promotion controls were disabled.

The Bot API nevertheless returned `can_restrict_members=true` for both channel
administrators. Telegram documents that `promoteChatMember` defaults this field
to true for promotions of channel administrators for backward compatibility.
Telegram Desktop exposes no independent broadcast-channel switch for the
field, so repeating the same operator action cannot produce the controller's
previously required value.

## Classification

This is a narrow Control-contract defect, not operator error, repository drift,
runtime drift or a product-boundary violation. The public runtime remained on
the unchanged source application throughout the failed preflight.

## Correction

The controller now:

- proves through `getChat` that the fixed target is a broadcast `channel`;
- requires the compatibility field to be present as a boolean;
- accepts either boolean value only for that channel type;
- continues to require change-info, post and edit rights;
- continues to reject anonymous administration, deletion, invitations,
  video-chat management, administrator promotion, stories and direct-message
  management.

No group or supergroup is accepted. No new Telegram capability, product route,
runtime service or data store is introduced.

## Recovery evidence

Before any server source or runtime mutation, a fresh scoped backup was created
at:

`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s8-public-telegram/20260904T110654Z-pre-s10-2b-public-telegram`

Its verified checksum-index SHA-256 is
`e096fd678a021ac9aae5d6a6c68c62187afe42743ca85bb5ee982b3190f8252f`.
It contains no Telegram token values.

Reference: `https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#promotechatmember`.
